    "result_text": "I've implemented `summarize_ticket` in `app/summary.py`. The existing tests pass (2 passed), but neither of them tests this function, so it hasn't been run against a model or a fake.\n\n```python\nmessages = [SystemMessage(content=SUMMARY_PROMPT), HumanMessage(content=ticket_text(ticket))]\nreply = chat.invoke(messages, stop=[\"\\n\\n\"])\nreturn str(reply.text).strip()\n```\n\n- **One request:** it makes a single `chat.invoke` call with the system message and the user message.\n- **Stop sequence:** it passes `stop=[\"\\n\\n\"]`, which is the standard `BaseChatModel` way to set one, so it works with any LangChain chat model.\n- **Plain string:** it reads the reply through `.text` rather than `str(message.content)`. Some models, such as Anthropic's, return content as a list of blocks, and `str()` on that list would give the list's text form instead of the reply. `.text` joins the text parts into one string. I used it as a property, since calling it as a method is deprecated in this version.\n\n`translate_replies` in `app/translate.py` uses `str(message.content)`, so it has the same list-of-blocks problem with those models. I left it alone because it's outside this task."
